    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/2a69c4c24bbb1003715e236687fd1bafed513996</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/ossf/malicious-packages/commit/2a69c4c24bbb1003715e236687fd1bafed513996"/>
    <title>
        Withdraw MAL-2026-17408 whalibmob (false positive) (#1670)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-10-27T11:07:27Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/295772194?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>vitaliichepurko-ox</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/vitaliichepurko-ox</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Withdraw MAL-2026-17408 whalibmob (false positive) (#1670)

The report claimed an injected auto-FOLLOW query (query_id 7871414976211147)
on connect. Re-review of all 20 listed versions (5.24.0 to 5.33.5) and the
current latest found no such query id, no call of joinNewsletter outside the
user-driven CLI command, no hardcoded or encoded channel targets and no
remote JID list. The package is not a Baileys fork.

Refs ossf/malicious-packages#1667

Signed-off-by: Vitalii Chepurko &amp;lt;vitalii.chepurko@ox.security&amp;gt;
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
